      "content": "Voluntary sensory deprivation can be an intense experience, and while some seek it for focus, extreme isolation can also lead to increased anxiety or hallucinations. Instead of immediate, long-term deprivation, you might consider structured sensory breaks, like short periods of deep quiet or nature exposure. These can help reduce external interference without the risks of total isolation. Always prioritize gradual exposure and have a safety plan in place before undertaking any intense detox period.",
